{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/843228-the-lancea-et-sanctum-and-hell","id":843228,"title":"The Lancea et Sanctum and Hell","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-06T18:35:28-08:00","id":843228,"title":"The Lancea et Sanctum and Hell","content":"I've been looking through the Testament of Longinus, the Second Edition corebook, and the old Covenant book for any clear statements about what they believe happens to the vampire soul after Final Death. I can't seem to find anything, though, so I'm going to just come out and ask. Do we have any information on what the Lancea et Sanctum tends to teach with regards to vampires and the afterlife? I know they call vampires Damned, but does this mean they're definitely all going to Hell no matter what they do? Is there a 'fulfill God's purpose for us and go to Heaven at the end' clause somewhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T18:46:11-08:00","id":843232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/843228-the-lancea-et-sanctum-and-hell#post843228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been looking through the Testament of Longinus, the Second Edition corebook, and the old Covenant book for any clear statements about what they believe happens to the vampire soul after Final Death. I can't seem to find anything, though, so I'm going to just come out and ask. Do we have any information on what the Lancea et Sanctum tends to teach with regards to vampires and the afterlife? I know they call vampires Damned, but does this mean they're definitely all going to Hell no matter what they do? Is there a 'fulfill God's purpose for us and go to Heaven at the end' clause somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, given that they're immortal and all, I always figured they believed that if they managed to live until Judgement Day, the righteous would go to heaven, the wicked would go to hell, and vampires would inherit the earth. But yeah, if you die before then, you are Damned. Hell awaits you.<br /> <br /> What's always interested me is what Sanctified who were embraced postmortem think of this. I imagine they would have a unique perspective on the concept of an afterlife, as compared to vampires who were immediately reanimated after death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T19:16:03-08:00","id":843244,"title":"","content":"In general, there's two schools of thought. One is that righteous vampires will get to rule over hell as a kind of Predator's paradise; all the sinners they could want to feed on for eternity. Second is a school that says that they'll be redeemed, lose their damnation, and go to heaven like everything else. There's no official consensus out there, and will change between cities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T19:31:29-08:00","id":843253,"title":"","content":"Lancea Sanctum, p52.<br /> <br /> 'The final chapters of Eschaton suggest that a vampire who fulfills the role for which God has chosen her and survives until the End of Days may seek absolution for all her sins. If her contrition is genuine, God will grant her absolution, thereby proving that His Infinite Grace is available to even the most corrupt and debased creatures. The vampire, now truly Sanctified, will ascend to Heaven as a reward for her acceptance of the burden of vampirism. The book cautions, however, that absolution will not be available to those who deny their vampiric natures. Those who believe that Humanity can be retained through personal willpower alone are guilty of the sin of Pride and will not be welcomed into the Kingdom of Heaven.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T07:34:47-08:00","id":843423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/843228-the-lancea-et-sanctum-and-hell?p=843253#post843253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lancea Sanctum, p52.<br /> <br /> 'The final chapters of Eschaton suggest that a vampire who fulfills the role for which God has chosen her and survives until the End of Days may seek absolution for all her sins. If her contrition is genuine, God will grant her absolution, thereby proving that His Infinite Grace is available to even the most corrupt and debased creatures. The vampire, now truly Sanctified, will ascend to Heaven as a reward for her acceptance of the burden of vampirism. The book cautions, however, that absolution will not be available to those who deny their vampiric natures. Those who believe that Humanity can be retained through personal willpower alone are guilty of the sin of Pride and will not be welcomed into the Kingdom of Heaven.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting yet supposedly theban encourages them to hold onto humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T07:55:27-08:00","id":843435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/843228-the-lancea-et-sanctum-and-hell?p=843423#post843423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting yet supposedly theban encourages them to hold onto humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell of a hair shirt, huh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 03-07-2016, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T08:59:00-08:00","id":843460,"title":"","content":"It may be more like the Circle of the Crone, appreciate humanity, not pretend you're human. It's another reason for them to align more with the Invictus than the Carthians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T09:27:25-08:00","id":843479,"title":"","content":"I think they key is &quot;through personal Willpower alone.&quot; It's probably fine if you believe your Faith and the Sanctum can help you? That is, your nature is a monster, and you shouldn't ever forget that, but the Sanctum can help you direct that in a good (to the Sanctum) way.<br /> <br /> But Sanctum fluff isn't my specialty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T12:45:03-08:00","id":843571,"title":"","content":"I heard somewhere that the afterlife doesn't prominently feature in Judaism. I don't know if that true, it isn't the sort of question you just can answer by glancing at Wikipedia after all, but it makes me wonder if the afterlife was significant to the early Lancea et Sanctum. If it wasn't, they could still adopt and adapt Christian beliefs over time, but without firm scriptural backing, they'd be up for debate.<br /> <br /> The humanity paradox does open questions about Theban sorcery. Maybe using it is <i>against</i> God's will, but who's going to argue with well established sorcerors? And when I heard about the Marian Apparition miracle, I thought it would very practical to use that on a frequent, ritual basis to keep the congregation stable. What's more, it's apparently dependent on more than personal will.<br /> <br /> And it's supposedly &quot;misunderstood&quot; because of its influence on Cruac (Sorry about the tangent). By whom? Fledglings? Acolyte and Dragon critics? Other Spear sects? If Cruac spread from the remnants of Blood-Blessed* in the British Isles, then perhaps Anglican and Non-conformist Spears who had moved away from saint devotion anyway were the ones said that the ritual was wrong based on its association. Now I imagine that a lot of modern Spears in this country would be relatively lax in the practices of the faith, possibly being mostly of the Westminster Creed but the ones who follow the anti-Marian school of thought <i>and</i> commit fervently to being monsters could be pretty messed up as Spears go.<br /> <br /> *amongst others, but I point out them because of their association with Mary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 03-07-2016, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T12:57:10-08:00","id":843578,"title":"","content":"The funny thing about Theban Sorcery is that, for as much as the Church tries to appeal to theological purity, heresies crop up all the time, and that's reflected in their magic. Livian heresy, the belial heresy. Hells, its clear in their modus operandus. Any time knowledge surfaces that dont' agree with the local doctrine? Search it out, grab it, wipe everything but the Lancea's copy, and that goes into deep storage.<br /> <br /> Vampires are all about control, and even God can't tell them what to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T13:27:30-08:00","id":843597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/843228-the-lancea-et-sanctum-and-hell?p=843578#post843578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The funny thing about Theban Sorcery is that, for as much as the Church tries to appeal to theological purity, heresies crop up all the time, and that's reflected in their magic. Livian heresy, the belial heresy. Hells, its clear in their modus operandus. Any time knowledge surfaces that dont' agree with the local doctrine? Search it out, grab it, wipe everything but the Lancea's copy, and that goes into deep storage.<br /> <br /> Vampires are all about control, and even God can't tell them what to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lancea et Sanctum's beliefs never made much sense to me on the whole. What I like about them is that is that it doesn't <i>have</i> to make sense for them to gain power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T14:17:48-08:00","id":843617,"title":"","content":"On a level, they're not supposed to make sense. One of the first things you'll notice about the Lancea Sanctum covenant book, back when it first came out, is that it mentions two things almost right off the bat.<br /> <br /> 1) The LeS offers easy answers that tend to fall apart on close examination<br /> 2) The LeS are hypocrites through and through. <br /> <br /> Lance doctrine is a mess of irreconsilable contradictions that you really can't put it into a coherant whole. Vampires are predators and should cull the weak of the human herd (ie sinners / criminals) to make the whole healthy. A bit later, the documents claim that everyone is a sinner, so everyone's blood is fair game. Even the moral and strong centers of communities. Any works made by vampires will be undone by their own nature, but the Church, despite being work of vampire hands, is supposed to last. Doctrine says both that vampires are Damned, and Blessed. The entire thing is a deliberate mess of contradiction and hypocracy. <br /> <br /> Now, from a game standpoint, that makes total sense. You want arguments over what is or isn't allowed. You want vying sects, you want mistranslations, you want the actually righteous and the sanctamonius asshats who justify attrocities with religion. <br /> <br /> To me, I tend to take an idealized view of the LeS when I play one. Forget blind zealotry. I play a vampire that actively believes that they are meant to hunt down criminal elements in the city. My character set themselves up as ideal victims for someone to mug or attack in some way, then turn the tables on the &quot;sinners.&quot; Corrupt politicians make a stable diet as well. God is not all love and kindness. God is the sword of justice, and the aegis of protection. God has been known as the Doer of Evil in some texts, implying that he commands some rather nasty things for the betterment of the whole. Ever hear of a vampire called a &quot;dark angel?&quot; That's what the LeS is to me when I play. An avenging angel that punishes the wicked, protects humanity. Preserves culture and knowledge through the ages. Hunts demons. To my characters, that's the simple message of the Testament. You are a necessary evil that preserves what is good. Fight darkness with darkness. Sure, you're an undead monster now. But you can still make this world a better place. That has a lot of appeal to a lot of people. And its something you can work with down the ages. No threat of ennui there. Just an eternity of good yet pleasurable works.<br /> <br /> That's the ideal anyways. As with most things vampire, corruption gets into the works, and gums up everything. Self justification and other excuses slip in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T18:39:34-08:00","id":843725,"title":"","content":"I think that's, as far as these things go, an ideal vision of the Lancea Et Sanctum. But important detail of this opinion: It's <i>an</i> ideal example, not <i>the</i> ideal form. The lovely thing about it is that their mainsteam beliefs as they exist can be aligned to more than one view that is coherent and also genuine in its message and carries a powerful meaning.<br /> <br /> And that's the other thing, it's just bloody fantastic that the Sanctum has all these irreconcilable contradictions and opposing turns and statements and mutually exclusive or hypocritical propositions within the same movements and sometimes even within the same documents. Not only because it provides so much alternative and distinction for the covenant within its premises, but because <i>real religions are like this too, go figure.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-07-2016, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}